s with suited tiles\n\nReason: Discarding J2 maintains maximum flexibility in my Bamboo suit, which forms the core of my hand with a completed pung (B4-B4-B4) and strong sequential potential (T1-T2-T3-T4-T4-T5). With 4 T4 tiles still unshown, I have excellent chances to complete a pung of T4's, which would give me a near-complete hand needing only one more tile. The J2 pair offers minimal scoring value compared to the suited tile combinations I can pursue.\n\nAnswer: Play J2"}
